1
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:27,677
Who are you?

2
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:29,760
Have you come from the real world?

3
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:32,257
That's right.

4
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:33,660
My name's Sinon.

5
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:39,400
Asuna sent me to save you and
Bercouli from Emperor Vecta.

6
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:43,940
I'm sorry I couldn't.

7
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:47,470
No.

8
00:00:47,553 --> 00:00:48,497
Do not be.

9
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:50,300
His death is my fault.

10
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:53,613
Were the others safe when you left them?

11
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:57,061
They were heading for some ruins,

12
00:00:57,560 --> 00:01:00,442
but the Red Knights from
my world are closing in.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,706
They'll catch up to him soon.

14
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:06,300
In that case, I must co-join them.

15
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:07,540
No, Alice.

16
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:09,320
You can't.

17
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:13,740
You need to keep heading south,
to the World's End Altar.

18
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:18,100
If you touch the console—I
mean, the crystal panel,

19
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:21,697
the people on the real-world
side will bring you to them.

20
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:22,800
Why should I?

21
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,441
Emperor Vecta is dead, is he not?

22
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:27,610
Sort of.

23
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:29,340
But it's not that simple.

24
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:33,580
If someone from the real world
dies here, they only die here.

25
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:36,160
In my world, they're still alive.

26
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:39,668
Vecta was a shell with
a real worlder in it.

27
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:43,000
You can destroy the shell, but the person,

28
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:46,084
the one inside, can come
back here if they want.

29
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:50,240
So the villain uncle
sacrificed himself to kill.

30
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:52,140
He's not really dead.

31
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:58,880
He has simply vanished and will awaken in
your world alive, as if nothing happened.

32
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:03,140
Was it all for nothing?

33
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:04,700
All this death?

34
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,960
Are you saying Uncle died in vain?

35
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:15,840
What kind of duel is it, where
only one risks their life?

36
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:18,297
That is no duel!

37
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:20,380
That is nothing but a farce!

38
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,940
You know, Kirito,

39
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:30,780
you don't think his intentions in
suffering are for nothing, do you?

40
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:35,520
He's from the real world too,
and it's the same for him.

41
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:38,380
If he died here, he wouldn't really die.

42
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:42,480
But still, like, everything
he felt here was real.

43
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:48,300
His wounds, the pain he suffered, the
damage to his soul, they're all real.

44
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:50,640
He's my friend.

45
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:52,400
I love him.

46
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:54,340
I care about him.

47
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:57,960
The same goes for Asuna
and so many other people,

48
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:01,435
and we're all hoping and
praying he pulls through this.

49
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:02,580
Back home,

50
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:07,329
none of us knew why he put himself
through so much in a world he wasn't from.

51
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:09,660
He did it for you, Alice.

52
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:15,320
All he wanted was to save you, and
that's real, as real as your uncle.

53
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:18,220
He fought with everything he had,

54
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:23,920
suffered all those wounds, and in the
end, he gave his life to save you.

55
00:03:32,060 --> 00:03:37,760
Sinon, if I leave through the World's
End Altar, what becomes of my family,

56
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,960
the people whom I love?

57
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:44,280
Will I be trapped there, or can I return?

58
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:46,520
You can, whenever.

59
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:49,730
her.

60
00:03:49,813 --> 00:03:51,637
As long as you and the
Underworld are both safe.

61
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:52,657
Very well then.

62
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:54,380
I shall head south for the

63
00:03:57,100 --> 00:03:57,930
altar.

64
00:03:58,013 --> 00:04:01,840
Part of me still resists this course
of action, but they both wished it.

65
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,840
Uncle, as well

66
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,190
as Kirito.

67
00:04:06,273 --> 00:04:08,336
You should go join the others though.

68
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:09,290
Hurry.

69
00:04:09,373 --> 00:04:12,660
If that Vecta guy comes back,
I think he'll come back here.

70
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:16,900
If he does, I'll keep him
busy, buy you a little time.

71
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:22,360
I appreciate it, and I swear your
efforts shall not be in vain.

72
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:53,040
...

73
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:05,380
The color of your soul is what
is the color of your soul?

74
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:19,735
What's the most important thing to me?

75
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:45,540
Thank you.

76
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:03,460
Oh, my God.

77
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:18,700
If this is how I die,

78
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:23,335
at least the previous champ won't
laugh when I see him in the afterlife.

79
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:44,540
Why does my heart hurt so
I just want to cut him?

80
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:57,657
I want to savor that battle again
feel it burn down to my core

81
00:07:57,740 --> 00:08:02,320
I want to sever those fists
which are harder than diamonds.

82
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:05,360
That was my only desire.

83
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:07,860
But this pain.

84
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:13,360
Slice and hack and slash away.

85
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:16,171
And at the end of your blood-smeared path,

86
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,760
you will find the key
to breaking your curse.

87
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:21,820
At least, you might.

88
00:08:23,900 --> 00:08:25,580
Ah, I see.

89
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:52,120
For your service, I thank you.

90
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:07,100
Thank you for yours as well, Yoyobi.

91
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:09,120
You are tired.

92
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:11,440
Go. Rest now.

93
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,880
Your sword broke. I'm sorry.

94
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:16,500
It's all my fault.

95
00:09:18,020 --> 00:09:18,850
No.

96
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:20,360
Do not trouble yourself.

97
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:25,240
At long last, I know why
I have this compulsion.

98
00:09:28,580 --> 00:09:30,997
To find what I don't want to slash.

99
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:33,477
To find what I want to protect.

100
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:36,120
I was fighting toward one goal.

101
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:39,320
That goal was you.

102
00:09:43,660 --> 00:09:44,580
Damn it.

103
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:47,900
I wish we could have
had a family together.

104
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:52,697
We could have had ourselves
the strongest kid ever.

105
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:55,620
way stronger than the previous champ.

106
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:57,600
Stronger than me.

107
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:01,040
The strongest pugilist of us all.

108
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:02,540
Hardly.

109
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:04,960
Our child would be a knight.

110
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:36,813
If we can keep the pressure on, this
will be wrapped up real soon, I hope.

111
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,340
You're the best.

112
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:40,717
I mean it.

113
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:42,960
I can't begin to thank you.

114
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:45,500
Oh, come on.

115
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:47,357
You don't have to thank anyone.

116
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:49,157
I owe you like nobody's business.

117
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:53,137
Heck you and kitty dude always
had my back it's the least

118
00:10:53,220 --> 00:11:00,097
I could do by the way um he
here he's safe in a wagon just

119
00:11:00,180 --> 00:11:03,917
down there after this is
over you should definitely go

120
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,412
talk to him maybe one of your
dumb jokes will wake him up?

121
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:11,640
Man, you're as harsh as ever.

122
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:19,737
It'll be okay.

123
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:21,320
I know it. Fast pants!

124
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:25,160
We'll pull through, I'm sure.

125
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:26,420
Damn straight!

126
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:31,640
Alrighty, let's switch back
in and finish this. Right.

127
00:11:34,660 --> 00:11:35,660
You okay?

128
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:39,597
I just saw someone...

129
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:40,657
up there.

130
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:43,211
Haven't we seen that guy somewhere before?

131
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:45,450
Hmm?

132
00:11:45,533 --> 00:11:46,700
He's too far away to tell.

133
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:49,537
And with his hood up, I can't...

134
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:51,660
see his... face.

135
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:56,997
Are you kidding?

136
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:58,380
There's no way!

137
00:11:58,780 --> 00:11:59,677
Not here!

138
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:02,320
Am I seeing... ghosts now?

139
00:12:03,140 --> 00:12:04,057
But that's crazy!

140
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:05,434
There's no such thing!

141
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,900
Well, look at him.

142
00:12:09,140 --> 00:12:10,280
That black cloak?

143
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:12,457
No, it's a leather poncho.

144
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:14,880
That's the leader of Laughing Coffin.

145
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,500
It's Pooh.

146
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:27,470
In here?

147
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:34,940
Look, it's the players from Japan.

148
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:44,377
No more.

149
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:46,317
Please God, no more!

150
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:49,057
Holy crap, we're in for it now!

151
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:51,577
This match ain't from America.

152
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:53,117
Or Japan.

153
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:54,880
We're so screwed.

154
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:57,900
They're from China and Korea!

155
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:17,080
I don't want to enlist.

156
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:21,382
If the army allowed
atmospheres, I wouldn't mind.

157
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:26,900
Links start.

158
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:45,360
A bunch of Korean, American, and
Chinese gamers made a new VR game.

159
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:49,940
And their test server has just been
hacked by a group of Japanese players.

160
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:52,773
They're attacking the testers right now.

161
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:55,997
Someone's always spoiling
someone else's fun.

162
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,300
Bunch of jerks.

163
00:13:58,640 --> 00:14:00,357
Those big dumb ones are the bad guys!

164
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:01,969
They must be the Japanese.

165
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:03,580
They look organized.

166
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:06,756
The big red ones must be the testers.

167
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:08,357
They're getting hammered.

168
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:09,560
Wait a sec.

169
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:12,922
The Japanese look like
they're fighting them off.

170
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,480
Hey, Amunfeiz.

171
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:25,526
Have you seen that video yet?

172
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:28,720
Yeah, Mei-Mei-Shang. Just now.

173
00:14:29,220 --> 00:14:31,040
It's crazy, huh? I'll say.

174
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:34,197
Hurry up and download the
client and let's get in there.

175
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:35,200
What client?

176
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:40,630
Oh.

177
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:45,380
Seeking volunteers to help save the testers
from the vicious Japanese attackers?

178
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:48,100
For anyone who'd like to join,

179
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:52,085
please download the required
client software to your atmosphere.

180
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:55,480
I'm still not sold on the
Japanese attackers' part.

181
00:14:55,980 --> 00:14:57,100
It's so weird.

182
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,820
Meixiang, what do you think?

183
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:01,037
This legit?

184
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:04,717
It I don't know yet
but if what they say is

185
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:07,457
true then our fellow gamers are in trouble

186
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:12,517
and could use all the help they can get
yeah I don't know about that it all sounds

187
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:17,857
fishy install the client and find out for
yourself I'm diving in now see if I see ya

188
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:22,997
I got nothing better to do it looks like a

189
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:25,551
bunch of my friends already dove in there.

190
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:40,320
It's him.

191
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:15,440
I know this guy, those
eyes, a face, I know him.

192
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:33,820
Son, I'm sorry.

193
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:57,017
Come in, Higa.

194
00:16:57,100 --> 00:16:58,100
You doing okay?

195
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:03,657
Yeah, so far.

196
00:17:03,740 --> 00:17:05,152
We should be there soon.

197
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:08,913
The bulkhead's maybe a couple
minutes down from us still.

198
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:10,270
Sounds good.

199
00:17:10,353 --> 00:17:11,882
When you get to it, let me know.

200
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:15,480
I'll tell the guys with
Ichiemon to send him in. Roger.

201
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:17,590
Hey, Yuna.

202
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:19,717
Thanks again for going with him.

203
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:22,740
I owe you big time when
this is over. You got it.

204
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,117
Holy crap, that's a lot of nerds.

205
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,847
How many are in there total?

206
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:32,840
What the hell?

207
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:36,022
It's the alarm for the bulkhead!

208
00:17:36,220 --> 00:17:38,097
Someone's gone and flipped the locks!

209
00:17:38,180 --> 00:17:40,886
Don't just stand there
and check the corridor!

210
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:52,810
Damn it!

211
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:54,737
The highjackers know about Ichiemon!

212
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:55,700
You there yet?

213
00:17:57,980 --> 00:18:00,277
We're almost to the maintenance connector.

214
00:18:00,360 --> 00:18:01,654
Ten more meters to go.

215
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:03,190
All right.

216
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:07,317
I'll keep an eye on Kirito's luck flight
and let you know if anything happened.

217
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:09,400
Good luck, Higa. Oh, hell.

218
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:17,362
Hey, Moonphase!

219
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:18,730
Now time.

220
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:20,214
What took you so long?

221
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:21,570
Sorry, guys.

222
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:23,505
I was getting ready for class.

223
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:29,140
So, uh, what do we do now?

224
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:31,060
The terrain looks sick.

225
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:33,658
Are those guys the Japanese players?

226
00:18:36,900 --> 00:18:38,240
Listen up, people!

227
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:43,580
I want to thank all of you for
diving in here and helping the cause.

228
00:18:44,440 --> 00:18:49,200
Bad news is, we're too late to save the
Alpha Testers in this part of the map.

229
00:18:49,620 --> 00:18:52,940
They were killed out by the
Japanese a little while ago.

230
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:54,320
But don't worry.

231
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:57,237
We got them logged back
in to another location,

232
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,557
and they're continuing
their work from there.

233
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:02,160
Since the Japanese hacked our server,

234
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:05,539
they got access to all the
high-spec gear they want.

235
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:09,400
They're also blocking us
devs from our admin access.

236
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:14,820
What that means is, we have
to fight using default gear!

237
00:19:15,580 --> 00:19:16,410
Cowards!

238
00:19:16,493 --> 00:19:17,852
Let's kick them all out!

239
00:19:18,380 --> 00:19:19,210
Yeah!

240
00:19:19,293 --> 00:19:20,731
Let's protect our server!

241
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:24,797
That's the spirit!

242
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:26,577
Patriots don't need fancy soldiers!

243
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:28,013
God, my head's ringing.

244
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:29,000
Mine too.

245
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:35,260
It's like my brains been taken over
hang on if he's really a devil he says

246
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:38,551
You could just cut the power to the server

247
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:00,680
Sit this one out, Asuna.

248
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:05,460
Let us have the glory
for once. He's right.

249
00:20:05,740 --> 00:20:07,799
We've been itching for a challenge.

250
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:08,930
Sheyta!

251
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:45,700
Claps!

252
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:47,670
Claps!

253
00:21:22,060 --> 00:21:24,820
Here it is, the maintenance connector.

254
00:21:33,240 --> 00:21:34,280
Matching in now.

255
00:21:46,620 --> 00:21:47,450
Yes!

256
00:21:47,620 --> 00:21:49,444
That was easier than I thought.

257
00:21:49,740 --> 00:21:52,260
I got Kirito's and Asuna's STLs.

258
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:54,439
And the two girls in Roppongi, too.

259
00:21:54,840 --> 00:21:56,080
We got this.

260
00:21:57,100 --> 00:21:58,060
Don't move!

261
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:00,337
Oh, oh,

262
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:07,420
oh.

263
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:18,557
How long have you

264
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:25,077
created a

265
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:26,000
